    {
      "text": "DESCRIPTION",
      "page_pdf": 23,
      "page_manual": "EVB-23",
      "section_code": "EVB",
      "label": "section_header",
      "bbox": [
        52.44,
        514.62824718,
        130.62018822000002,
        504.48154166300554
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Li-ion battery controller (LBC) monitors the status of the inside of the Li-ion battery at all times and sends information, such as the charging status of Li-ion battery and possible power, to VCM (vehicle control module) via EV system CAN communication.",
      "page_pdf": 23,
      "page_manual": "EVB-23",
      "section_code": "EVB",
      "label": "text",
      "bbox": [
        53.46000999999998,
        501.11592,
        559.944186400001,
        468.8324008640884
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Li-ion battery controller performs control as per the following.",
      "page_pdf": 23,
      "page_manual": "EVB-23",
      "section_code": "EVB",
      "label": "text",
      "bbox": [
        53.46001000000001,
        466.6160004,
        355.3806340000004,
        457.3724128640884
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Monitors the battery state and transfers chargeable/dischargeable power to VCM to prevent an error, such as overvoltage, over discharge or excessive temperature rise in the battery.",
      "page_pdf": 23,
      "page_manual": "EVB-23",
      "section_code": "EVB",
      "label": "list_item",
      "bbox": [
        53.46001000000001,
        455.0966088,
        559.7782948,
        434.3324812640884
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Detects an error (overvoltage, over discharge, overcurrent, or excessive temperature rise) immediately at the time of error occurrence and requests VCM to disconnect the system main relay to interrupt the discharge/charge line.",
      "page_pdf": 23,
      "page_manual": "EVB-23",
      "section_code": "EVB",
      "label": "list_item",
      "bbox": [
        53.46001000000004,
        432.1160808,
        559.9325980000004,
        399.8325616640884
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Maintains the optimum battery state constantly with a cell capacity adjustment function to prevent a reduction in charging/discharging capacity caused by cell capacity variations.",
      "page_pdf": 23,
      "page_manual": "EVB-23",
      "section_code": "EVB",
      "label": "list_item",
      "bbox": [
        53.46001000000004,
        397.6161612,
        559.8520011999997,
        376.8531820640884
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Detects the connector fit state with the function to detect the fit of the high voltage harness connector and transfers the detected state to VCM so that the vehicle does not start with an unsteady state.",
      "page_pdf": 23,
      "page_manual": "EVB-23",
      "section_code": "EVB",
      "label": "list_item",
      "bbox": [
        53.46084520000002,
        374.57622960000003,
        559.8718371999997,
        353.8726540640884
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Detects the insulation resistance state with the function to detect the insulation resistance between high and low voltage and transfers the detected state to VCM so that the vehicle does not start with an unusual state.",
      "page_pdf": 23,
      "page_manual": "EVB-23",
      "section_code": "EVB",
      "label": "list_item",
      "bbox": [
        53.46105399999999,
        351.59570160000004,
        559.868913999999,
        330.8327224640884
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Estimates a battery charge state and low battery state, based on the data obtained with the battery state detection function, and reflects on the battery capacity meter.",
      "page_pdf": 23,
      "page_manual": "EVB-23",
      "section_code": "EVB",
      "label": "list_item",
      "bbox": [
        53.461262799999986,
        328.616322,
        559.8230823999995,
        307.8533428640884
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "BATTERY PROTECTION",
      "page_pdf": 23,
      "page_manual": "EVB-23",
      "section_code": "EVB",
      "label": "section_header",
      "bbox": [
        52.44,
        299.64826718,
        182.68221144929996,
        289.50156166300553
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Li-ion  battery  has  a  voltage  range  capable  of  charge/discharge.  If  charged/discharged  exceeding  the range, excessive low capacity or malfunction may be caused. To prevent this, the Li-ion battery controller detects voltage of each cell and requests the control of charging/discharging energy to VCM so that the cell voltage stays within the voltage range.",
      "page_pdf": 23,
      "page_manual": "EVB-23",
      "section_code": "EVB",
      "label": "text",
      "bbox": [
        53.46001,
        286.1359,
        559.9251856,
        242.3935412640883
      ]
    },
