      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "During cell capacity adjustment, the capacity of each cell is estimated based on the no-load voltage when the system starts, and the capacities are adjusted so that they are all at the target level. The voltage of each cell is detected inside the Li-ion battery controller. The bypass switches are then turned ON to discharge the cells that have excess capacity. In this way, capacity adjustment by the Li-ion battery controller allows the capacity of all cells to be fully utilized.",
      "page_pdf": 24,
      "page_manual": "EVB-24",
      "section_code": "EVB",
      "label": "text",
      "bbox": [
        52.139999999999986,
        722.33589,
        558.596928,
        667.1323948640886
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "INSULATION RESISTANCE LOSS DETECTION FUNCTION",
      "page_pdf": 24,
      "page_manual": "EVB-24",
      "section_code": "EVB",
      "label": "section_header",
      "bbox": [
        52.14,
        474.24827718,
        361.5125963583999,
        464.10157166300553
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The insulation resistance detection circuit mounted inside the Li-ion battery controller measures the insulation resistance of each high voltage part and sends the measurement results to VCM via EV system CAN communication.",
      "page_pdf": 24,
      "page_manual": "EVB-24",
      "section_code": "EVB",
      "label": "text",
      "bbox": [
        52.139999999999986,
        460.73591,
        558.5353319999998,
        428.4523908640884
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "VCM judges abnormal insulation resistance in each high voltage part, based on the received insulation resistance value.",
      "page_pdf": 24,
      "page_manual": "EVB-24",
      "section_code": "EVB",
      "label": "text",
      "bbox": [
        52.139999999999986,
        426.1754384,
        558.5217600000012,
        405.4718628640884
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "LI-ION BATTERY HEATER CONTROL SYSTEM",
